
Running just the simulation (from the command line):
  mic W26_following

Also plotting the files (requires gnuplot, first calls mic; then gnuplot):
  W26_following.run

Changing the model parameters
(only one vehicle type, if more, we would have also W26_following.W262 etc)"
  edit W26_following.W261
  use_vl=1 => "rectangular" Wiedemann loops
  use_vl=0 => "oblique" Wiedemann loops

Inspect/edit leader profile (linearly interpolated, constant extrapolated)
  edit W26_following.vlead1

  Example:  only the line 120   10 => always v_lead=10 m/s
  Example2: addtl line 125   6 => v_lead=10 m/s for t<120 s, 
  v_lead=6 m/s for t>125 s, and linear interpolation for t in [120,125] s  

Inspect/edit initial configuration:
  edit W26_following.ICsingle
  
  => 17 cars i=0,...,16 are simulated with given initial positions and speeds 
     i=0 irrelevant (bookkeeping, always prviding a defined gap)
     i=1=externally controlled leader (defined in file .leadvehs 
     i=2=test car making the loops in the s-dv diagram
     i>3 more followers to test string stability 